# Cloud Agents + remote continuity (Eric preference, Nov 2026)

Eric is often away from the primary Mac for weeks. Treat **git remote** as the handoff surface.

## Always

1. When a unit of work is finished (fix, feature slice, or explicit stop), **commit and `git push -u origin HEAD`** before claiming done — even if deploy is blocked. Another PC or Cloud Agent must be able to pick up from GitHub without this machine.
2. Prefer a dedicated worktree/branch (`.claude/worktrees/<slug>`). Never leave finished work only on a dirty local tree.
3. Do **not** assume this Mac's `.env.local` or `.vercel/` exist on a Cloud Agent VM. Cloud work that needs secrets must use repo-documented env vars / Vercel project link / Eric-supplied secrets — or stop and report the gap instead of inventing credentials.

## Prefer Cloud Agents when

- Eric asks for cloud / away / another PC / "continue without this computer"
- The task will outlast the current session (long test/fix/ship loops)
- Parallel investigation that should survive chat disconnect

Launch via Task with `environment: "cloud"` and `cloud_base_branch` set to a **pushed** remote branch (usually `main` or the feature branch under work). Unpushed local commits are invisible to cloud.

## After a Cloud Agent finishes

- Link the agent with `[Name](id)` and `[Review](bc-id#changes)` when it edited code
- Push is the cloud agent's job; verify the branch exists on `origin` before telling Eric it is portable
- Merge into the session branch only if Eric asked; otherwise leave the cloud branch for review

## Dashboard setup Eric still owns once

Cursor → Cloud Agents → environment (e.g. `mindy data core`) must list repo `ecoffie/market-assassin`. Blank Repositories = cloud runs cannot clone.
